Privacy Policy for Mitr
Effective Date: November 2, 2026

Last Updated: November 2, 2026

Welcome to Mitr (“Mitr,” “we,” “our,” or “us”). This Privacy Policy explains how we collect, use, disclose, and safeguard your personal data when you use the Mitr mobile application and related web services (collectively, the “Platform”).

Mitr operates in accordance with applicable Indian laws, including the Digital Personal Data Protection Act, 2023 (DPDP Act) and the Information Technology Act, 2000 along with its relevant rules. By creating an account or using Mitr, you consent to the data practices described in this policy.

1. Information We Collect
We collect information necessary to deliver, personalize, and secure your experience on Mitr:

A. Information You Provide Directly
Account Credentials: Name, mobile phone number, email address, date of birth, username, profile photo, and password or OTP authentication data.

Profile & Identity Details: Bio, language preferences, location (city/state), and government identity details if you choose to apply for a verified creator badge.

User-Generated Content: Posts, comments, messages, photos, videos, audio clips, poll votes, and interest tags you share across circles.

Customer Support & Communications: Records of queries, reports, or feedback sent to our support or grievance redressal team.

B. Information Collected Automatically
Usage & Interaction Data: Posts viewed, liked, or shared; accounts followed; circles joined; dwell time; and search history.

Device & Log Data: Device model, operating system version, unique device identifiers, IP address, network carrier, browser type, crash reports, and system performance logs.

Precise & Approximate Location: Coarse location derived from IP address or precise GPS data (only when explicitly enabled via device permissions for regional discovery).

C. Optional Device Permissions (Requested Explicitly)
Camera & Microphone: To record and post videos, photos, or voice notes.

Storage/Media Library: To upload photos, audio, and video files from your device.

Contacts: To help you find friends already on Mitr (processed with your explicit permission and never sold to third parties).

2. How We Use Your Information
We process personal data for legitimate purposes, including to:

Set up, manage, and authenticate your account.

Deliver localized feeds, regional language translations, and interest-based recommendations.

Facilitate real-time messaging, comments, and community interactions.

Enforce our Community Guidelines, detect harassment, spam, bots, or illegal content, and maintain a safe platform.

Monitor performance, fix bugs, and optimize app speed and responsiveness.

Comply with legal obligations, court orders, and government directives under Indian law.

3. Data Sharing and Disclosures
We do not sell your personal data. We disclose information only under the following circumstances:

Public Visibility: Your public profile, posts, comments, follower counts, and shared media are visible to other users according to your account privacy settings.

Service Providers: Trusted third-party vendors who provide cloud hosting, SMS delivery, analytics, content moderation, and technical infrastructure under strict data protection agreements.

Legal and Regulatory Authorities: Law enforcement agencies, courts, or regulatory bodies when mandated by valid legal processes under Indian law.

Business Transfers: In the event of a merger, acquisition, reorganization, or sale of assets, user data may be transferred subject to the recipient adhering to this Privacy Policy.

4. User Rights and Choices (Under DPDP Act)
As a user, you have specific rights regarding your personal data:

Right to Access & Correction: Access your personal data or update inaccurate/incomplete details directly within the app settings.

Right to Erasure & Account Deletion: Request complete deletion of your account and associated personal data at any time via Settings > Account > Delete Account.

Right to Withdraw Consent: Revoke permissions (e.g., location, microphone, contacts) at any time through your device settings.

Right of Grievance Redressal: Lodge complaints regarding personal data handling directly with our designated Grievance Officer.

Right to Nominate: Nominate an individual to exercise your data rights in the event of death or incapacity.

5. Data Security and Retention
Security Safeguards: We deploy industry-standard technical and organizational security controls, including encryption in transit (TLS/HTTPS), access controls, and regular vulnerability audits.

Data Retention: We retain your personal data only as long as your account remains active or as required to fulfill the purposes outlined in this policy. Upon account deletion, personal identifiers are erased or anonymized within 30 days, except where retention is legally mandated.

6. Protection of Minors
Mitr is intended for users aged 18 and above. Users between the ages of 13 and 17 may use the platform only with verifiable parental or legal guardian consent. We do not knowingly track, target, or process data of minors for targeted advertising.

7. Changes to This Privacy Policy
We may update this Privacy Policy to reflect platform features, security improvements, or regulatory changes. Material changes will be communicated via in-app notifications or registered email prior to taking effect.

